course: dictionary
lesson: 3585
title: Fibrosis: when tissue turns tough
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fibrosis is a doctor's word. It means too much tough, thick tissue grows in a part of the body, such as the lungs. Tissue is the material our bodies are made from, and this kind of tissue is like scar tissue.
explain: Context helps. «Cystic fibrosis is an inherited condition (passed down from parents)» tells you fibrosis is part of the name of an illness. The brackets explain that inherited means passed down from parents.
explain: «With thick sticky mucus (slime) in the lungs and gut» shows what can happen. When tissue turns stiff, an organ cannot work as well as it should. Look for clues like stiff and not work well to understand a hard word.
fact: Fibrosis means too much tough, thick tissue, like scar tissue, growing in part of the body.
fact: When this tissue grows in the lungs, the lungs become stiff and may not work as well.
fact: «Cystic fibrosis» is an inherited condition, passed down from parents, with thick sticky mucus in the lungs and gut.
fact: Cystic fibrosis is treated with medicines and daily chest physio, and it is not catching.
fact: «Pulmonary fibrosis» means scarring of the lungs, and it is mostly talked about in grown-ups.
exercise: «Cystic fibrosis is an inherited condition (passed down from parents).» What does inherited mean? | *Passed down from parents | Very old | Kept secret | Caught from other people
exercise: «With thick sticky mucus (slime) in the lungs and gut.» What does mucus mean here? | *Slime | Bone | Air | Blood
exercise: Ella says cystic fibrosis is catching, like a cold. What is the right answer? | Yes, it spreads like a cold | *No, it is not catching | Only in summer | Yes, from sharing a drink
test: Fibrosis makes tissue grow too much in a part of the body, such as the lungs. Which body part is given as an example? | *Lungs | Hair | Knees | Ears
test: What does fibrosis do to an organ when tissue turns stiff? | *Makes it stiff, so it may not work as well | Makes it lighter and softer | Makes it brighter in colour | Makes it faster and stronger
exam: «Pulmonary fibrosis» means what? | A heart test | A kind of cold | *Scarring of the lungs | Scarring of the skin
